      "writtenOn": "2024-05-22T09:01:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t encountered the problem in real. Looking through the code, I discovered that in the loop variable length is decremented and compared with zero and the index variable x is incremented by 4. Example of out-of-bounds code:\n\n    #include \u003cstdint.h\u003e\n    #include \u003cstdio.h\u003e\n\n    static int HasAlpha32b_C(const uint8_t* src, int length) {\n            int x;\n            for (x \u003d 0; length-- \u003e 0; x +\u003d 4) // if (src[x] !\u003d 0xff) return 1;\n                    printf(\"%d \", x);\n            return 0;\n    }\n\n    int main()\n    {\n            #define SRC_LEN 16\n            uint8_t data[SRC_LEN];\n            return HasAlpha32b_C(data, SRC_LEN);\n    }\n\nThis code outputs: 0 4 8 12 16 20 24 28 32 36 40 44 48 52 56 60",
      "revId": "1c07273b12df55d3fdc1ca80ea9aa8de2e646844",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
